<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:27Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0384bc82c07c766722801ee7d0cf7b9f805a3e8e378ba8a51f01d0c6513c25f</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--caf8d0ba14ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. People forget that, over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin BER airport Terminal 1 evacuated after security scare</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f0d6bb84984ec72867ff56cced330f14321a07818e6f4ecf622092819f42a66</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-evacuated-after-security-scare/a-78895207--2eb93a91d0a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-ber-airport-terminal-1-evacuated-after-security-scare/a-78895207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have emptied Terminal 1 at BER airport in Berlin, at least as a precaution. The airport said that more than two-dozen flights had been delayed but that they were trying to avoid any cancellations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia to close branches of Germany's Goethe-Institut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f396ab4a42233ffd1a3351b59e911a90e49c111c7eaee240faaebc47908e481</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T03:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-to-close-branches-of-germany-s-goethe-institut/a-78815269--2671655c2e1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-to-close-branches-of-germany-s-goethe-institut/a-78815269?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov said the move was in response to Germany's decision to close the Russian House in Berlin after blaming Moscow for an attemped drone attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU summons Russian envoy over failed Leipzig drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6937b5a552e0b796ac45ff61a6a5619c53c5b4aa665ea1e25cfd3daa8faf5394</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280--91d3b884dfe8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summons-russian-envoy-over-failed-leipzig-drone-attack/a-78687280?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said the attempted attack had "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism." She said the EU was summoning a Russian envoy, with France announcing a similar step.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police probe suspected power station attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46f6aaa4cb6cfbc423b493cb216a9225187dd081937d1c22ba6aa6e9b23135b9</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T06:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-suspected-power-station-attacks/live-78669282--f7474e797acc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-probe-suspected-power-station-attacks/live-78669282?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are investigating after homemade projectiles were used to damage power lines in eastern Germany. This comes amid suspicion of sabotage at another power station in the west of the country. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany says Russia behind attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3791a648bdf0cf1eadb611f5cbd887923b5c0a1e98607fe3585e107bbf60641c</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589--b38376dc9663.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-says-russia-behind-attempted-drone-attack-at-leipzig-airport/a-78584589?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators believe an explosives-laden drone was deliberately targeting a Ukrainian cargo aircraft at Leipzig/Halle airport in early August. The German government said on Tuesday that it held Russia "responsible."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's economic slump finally over?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0e7aa07df48aaa848b632d0c2063efee1eeaa4b1a9b983b051f87f4e6edbe5c</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447--a7b7320d701b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a slew of negative headlines, the German economy has posted its best figures in years. There are reasons for optimism, but structural issues remain.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Data centers are everywhere. Here's what they're doing to the planet.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a2248471a24bc4ad0a5979e7236b14676b53fb8d851d3d318f3d915e457e1d2</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/data-centers-are-everywhere-here-s-what-they-re-doing-to-the-planet/a-78789889--298e057664a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/data-centers-are-everywhere-here-s-what-they-re-doing-to-the-planet/a-78789889?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As data centers multiply to meet AI demand, they're straining power grids, draining water supplies, and reshaping the land and air around them.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin's punitive measures unlikely to deter Putin: experts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6686f7b76ee7a7f5c69a6b07e5fab50e0dca3f9968534eff13388e7fc2deaec5</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-punitive-measures-unlikely-to-deter-putin-experts/a-78803217--e7ac43c2d794.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-punitive-measures-unlikely-to-deter-putin-experts/a-78803217?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has announced punitive measures after publicly blaming Russia for an attempted airport drone attack. But a former diplomat, political and security analysts warn it will likely do little to deter the Kremlin.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: How to woo voters with an immigrant background</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbef672fc710766de080d982badc1e0c242ecfc0fad65ae2c3f2312ef4e8af13</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775--5e7baf534d71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-how-to-woo-voters-with-an-immigrant-background/a-78790775?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of voters in Germany with an immigrant background is rising. Yet the established parties barely manage to reach them. Why not?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4765e6e6fad7586d29435c2658a2374d09b1ecddc0a542b7f9c814c2fb9465ab</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--d7968a32f7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92c2db82dae4a4580ce0ad6671f3326ef7b9f59bff909dbcfa0c52487272de87</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--3ab5f0359b92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ea5c43f16912fc8d07b404b180c35c27c0bd22aca18731970cfbc678a785db0</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--c7c332adab8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
